    {
      "h": 40,
      "id": "rfd4c7138c",
      "llm_prompt_override": "You are a strict ID extractor for one OCR ROI field.\nYou are NOT reading an image. You only receive OCR-extracted text for the ID box.\nReturn ONE valid JSON object only, no markdown and no extra text.\nRequired output schema:\n{\"detected_text\":\"string or null\"}\n\nTarget ID format:\nExactly 7 digits followed by A or B, for example 7011606A or 8011638B.\n\nRules:\n1. If OCR text is JSON and key \"id\" exists, inspect that value first.\n2. From the chosen text, extract only a complete ID token matching ^[0-9]{7}[AB]$.\n3. Strip surrounding labels such as \"Record ID:\", \"ID:\", \"Student ID\", quotes, colons, and whitespace.\n4. If the text contains exactly one complete matching ID token, return it exactly as the 8-character token.\n5. If there are multiple matching tokens, or none, return {\"detected_text\":null}.\n6. Do not repair OCR mistakes: do not convert / to B, 8 to B, O to 0, I/l to 1, U to 0, or add/delete characters.\n7. Reject internal pipeline IDs such as p702:r1:id; never return them.\n8. Reject dates, page numbers, answer choices, form labels, school names, teacher names, and explanatory text.\n9. Do not add any extra keys or text.",
      "name": "id",
      "w": 270,
      "x": 44,
      "y": 12,
      "llm_field_data_type": "id",
      "llm_validation_rules": "Must be exactly 7 digits followed by A or B, or null.",
      "ocr_output_regex": "^[0-9]{7}[AB]$"
    },
    {
      "h": 34,
      "id": "r295803dcd",
      "llm_prompt_override": "You are a strict date extractor for one OCR ROI field.\nYou are NOT reading an image. You only receive OCR-extracted text for the date box.\nReturn ONE valid JSON object only, no markdown and no extra text.\nRequired output schema:\n{\"detected_text\":\"string or null\"}\n\nTarget date format:\nMM/DD/YYYY, with a four-digit year from 2000 through 2099.\nThe final detected_text must match this regex exactly:\n^(0[1-9]|1[0-2])/(0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|3[01])/(20[0-9]{2})$\n\nRules:\n1. Extract only the date written in this ROI.\n2. If OCR text contains a date with a two-digit year YY, interpret it as 20YY only when the month and day are clear.\n3. Zero-pad one-digit month or day.\n4. Return only a valid date-shaped value in MM/DD/YYYY that matches the regex above.\n5. If the date is missing, ambiguous, unreadable, incomplete, or cannot be made to match the regex using only visible OCR evidence, return null as {\"detected_text\":null}.\n6. Do not invent missing digits, do not guess a date from context, and do not use page numbers, IDs, question numbers, or form labels.\n7. Reject impossible or malformed OCR dates such as 02/80/2026, 04/79/2026, 0413126, 04/13, or 04/13/1926 by returning null.\n8. Do not add any extra keys or text.",
      "name": "date",
      "w": 229,
      "x": 192,
      "y": 212,
      "llm_field_data_type": "date",
      "llm_validation_rules": "Must match ^(0[1-9]|1[0-2])/(0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|3[01])/(20[0-9]{2})$ exactly, or null.",
      "ocr_output_regex": "^(0[1-9]|1[0-2])/(0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|3[01])/(20[0-9]{2})$"
    },
    {
